# -- how the window is dressed ---------------------------------------------
#
# Material Design 3, calculated from the accent colour of the desktop.
# material.py converts that one colour into tonal ladders and roles with
# names. This is the half that needs tkinter: it converts the roles into ttk
# styles, and it draws the shapes that ttk cannot draw.
#
# Two ideas of Material do most of the visible work. First, a raised surface
# is a lighter *tone* and not a border or a shadow. A window can then hold
# twelve groups of controls without twelve boxes around them. Second, hover,
# press and disabled use one mechanism: a layer of the content colour over the
# container. A colour for each widget is not necessary, and each control then
# changes by the same amount.

# The shape scale of Material, at the sizes of this window. A radius gives the
# size of an element: a full round end for a button, a soft corner for a
# panel, and a very small corner for a text field.
